If when you run gftodvi you get a warning like

    Sorry, I can't make diagonal rules of slant    0.16667!

then add this argument in the end of the command:

    'slantfont slant16667'

============================================================

For TeXbook p.23, run:
  dvi+ texput

For TeXbook p.26, run:
  dvi+ story

For TeXbook p.27, run:
  dvi+ story

For TeXbook p.30, run:
  dvi+ story

For TeXbook p.34, run:
  dvi+ story

For METAFONTbook p.32, run:
  gftodvi mfput.2602gf
  dvi- mfput

For METAFONTbook p.37, run:
  gftodvi io.2602gf
  dvi+ io

For METAFONTbook p.38, run:
  gftodvi io.2602gf
  dvi- io

For METAFONTbook p.39, no need to ask a local system wizard for help.
Instead, on the next page use the font directly from current directory:
  ./io scaled 4000

For METAFONTbook p.40, run:
  dvi- testfont

============================================================

texbook.tex and mfbook.tex are before 2021 tuneup

texbook.pdf and mfbook.pdf are after 2021 tuneup

=============================================================

How to compile texbook (mfbook is the same):
-\loop\iftrue
+\loop\iffalse
   \errmessage{This manual is copyrighted and should not be TeXed}\repeat
-\pausing1 \input manmac
+\pausing0 \input manmac
+\proofmodefalse
...
-\font\pearsonkluj=arial at 9pt
-\leftline{\pearsonkluj ScoutAutomatedPrintCode}
tex texbook
dvipdfmx -q -p 14.45cm,20cm -x 1.1cm -y 0pt texbook

